   "daf": "31b",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "וְלֹא בְּקַרְדּוֹם. אָמַר רַב חִינָּנָא בַּר שֶׁלֶמְיָא מִשְּׁמֵיהּ דְּרַב: לֹא שָׁנוּ אֶלָּא בְּנַקְבוּת שֶׁלּוֹ, אֲבָל בְּזַכְרוּת שֶׁלּוֹ — מוּתָּר.",
   "en": "It is taught in the mishna that even when it is permitted to chop wood on a Festival, one may «not» do so «with an ax. Rav Ḥinnana bar Shelemya said in the name of Rav: They taught» this prohibition «only» with regard to a case where one chops «with its female» side, i.e., the broad side of the ax, as was normally done. «But» if one chops «with its male» side, i.e., the narrow side, this «is permitted» because it is an unusual manner of chopping."
  }
 ],
